Subject: [PATCH] 1454 (b) / BQ: the server's plan sentence can name whom it
 introduces (OFF)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 53498, run 2: when the model's own plan sentence is not clean, the
server's D663 sentence stands in. It does not say whom the introduction
is to. The plan's route already carries the person to meet (BF, §128,
`introduction.to_name`; 14 of the last 25 plan calls fill it), so
nothing new goes to the model.

introTargetSentence.ts builds D739's form from the plan call: the
go-between in the genitive and the ergative, then the person to meet.
It applies only when the plan names exactly one reachable go-between and
one person to meet through them. planReplyText uses it in place of the
D663 sentence on the introduction path.

New words the owner reads, so INTRO_TARGET_SENTENCE_ON is false until
Misho's yes on the exact text (NIGHT_QUESTIONS BQ). Georgian only;
en/ru/es keep the D663 sentence. With the switch off nothing changes.

